---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base
    title="Company, KYDE"
    description="Kyde builds behavioral scoring for AI agents. Agents are attacked around the clock and can go wrong on their own, and in both cases every single action is allowed. Kyde learns how each agent behaves and catches the one that no longer behaves like itself. Engineered in Germany."
>
    <Navbar />

    <main>

        <!-- ══════════ HERO ══════════ -->
        <section data-surface="blush" class="page-hero relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="bg-grid absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none"></div>
            <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 pt-36 pb-24 md:pt-48 md:pb-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">

                <p class="hero-label">(Company)</p>

                <h1 class="hero-h1 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-bold text-ink-0 uppercase tracking-tight md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
                    Agents act in your name. We watch how they behave.
                </h1>
                <p class="mt-8 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
                    Kyde is behavioral scoring for AI agents. We learn how each agent normally behaves, score every run against it, and raise the alarm when an agent stops behaving like itself.
                </p>

            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ══════════ BODY ══════════ -->
        <section class="relative">
            <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[200px_1fr] gap-8 items-start">

                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-ink-0">About</p>
                        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink-1">[KYDE]</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-8 max-w-2xl">
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            AI agents now move money, answer customers, change code and touch data. They are attacked around the clock: manipulated documents, injected instructions, fraud aimed at the agent instead of the person. And they can go wrong on their own: after a model update, in a loop, or when they lose track of the task.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            In both cases every single action is allowed. The agent uses real credentials and real tools, so access control has nothing to object to. The only question left is whether the agent still behaves like itself.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            That is what Kyde measures. Deterministic statistics, no language model in the verdict, and every score can be recomputed by the customer or an auditor. Companies that need to stop an agent, not only see it, run the Kyde Gateway in their own network: the agent goes into quarantine, a human decides what happens next, and every action lands in a signed record.
                        </p>

                        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            Early stage. Engineered in Germany. We work with teams that run agents in production, starting with agents that move money.
                        </p>

                        <div class="pt-4">
                            <a
                                href="mailto:hello@kyde.com"
                                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-line-0 px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-1 hover:border-line-1 hover:text-ink-0 transition-all"
                            >
                                hello@kyde.com
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    <Footer />
</Base>
